Overlay patch 0053 (D20, port of SoH D-081): TOUCH DRAG-LOOK FOR THE MANUAL CAMERA.

A touch that lands on empty overlay space turns SM64's Manual (analog) camera
by finger travel. The shell (app/ios/SohIosShell.m) owns the gesture and
accumulates the travel in RIGHT-STICK UNITS; this patch is the game side, two
small __IOS__-gated hunks (the desktop build is byte-for-byte unchanged):

  1. game_init.c read_controller_inputs -- THE INJECTION POINT. Once per game
     tick, after adjust_analog_stick has turned player 1's raw right stick into
     stick2X/stick2Y (deadzone + 64 clamp), the shell's accumulated drag is
     drained and ADDED to stick2X/stick2Y. A drag therefore is a right-stick
     deflection proportional to drag speed, and everything downstream treats it
     exactly like one: mode_custom_camera turns sModeOffsetYaw by
     ANALOG_AMOUNT * stick2X/32 * CAMERA_SPEED (the port's Invert Horizontal
     and Camera Speed apply), lakitu_zoom moves sLakituPitch from stick2Y when
     Vertical Analog Camera is on (Invert Vertical applies), and an active
     stick suppresses the C-button rotation as upstream intends. stick2X/Y
     have no other consumer in this pin (only camera.c reads them; player 3's
     copy below is unused). Added after the clamp on purpose: a fast swipe may
     exceed full stick deflection (the shell caps one tick at 45 degrees and
     carries the rest). Skipped during demo playback (camera.c ignores the
     stick then anyway).

     Why not the SDL right-stick axes: LUS maps SDL RIGHTX/RIGHTY to BOTH the
     C-buttons and the N64 right stick, so driving drag-look through them would
     fire C presses (C-up = first-person view).

  2. camera.c mode_custom_camera -- INSTRUMENTATION + GATE. After the right
     stick's yaw is applied, report the tick to the shell
     (GsIos_ManualCamTick): it publishes sModeOffsetYaw/sLakituPitch for the
     bridge `look` command, logs (rate-limited) when the tick carried a touch
     delta, and its timestamp is the shell's "Manual camera live" gate -- so
     drag-look claims empty-space touches only while the analog camera
     actually runs (DefaultMode = Manual, or AlternateMode = Manual with R
     toggled; never in Lakitu/Mario modes, cutscenes, C-up or cannon).

Touch C-buttons are NOT masked off the right stick here (SoH 0062 masks
them): upstream's mode_custom_camera documents that the right stick is
commonly mapped to the C-buttons and deliberately prefers the stick, so a
touch C swinging the Manual camera at the analog rate is the intended
behaviour on this port (D20).


--- a/src/game/game_init.c
